7e752734-3fef-4ccf-b7a4-720c8ddfca41	committee_member	How are you different from MyGate? They charge high subscription and gateway fees.	FLATBRIZ offers a distinct advantage over MyGate by eliminating payment gateway commissions on maintenance collections. While MyGate typically routes payments through a gateway that takes a commission on every transaction, FLATBRIZ utilizes a UPI-first collection method that incurs zero gateway fees. This means that more of the funds collected stay within your society's corpus, enhancing financial transparency and control. Additionally, FLATBRIZ maintains robust visitor management features, including a Visitor tab and pre-approved Gate Passes, ensuring you don’t lose functionality while gaining better financial tools. \n\nWould you like to explore how FLATBRIZ can specifically address your society's needs?	12	{objection:payment_gateway_lag,competitor:mygate}	f	2026-09-15 05:21:16.083
df5db538-ce1a-49bf-9471-94ed2019248c	committee_member	Can we get a side-by-side cost comparison against what our society spends today?	Absolutely, a side-by-side cost comparison is a great way to evaluate FLATBRIZ against your current expenses. It's important to consider the total cost, not just the subscription fee. For instance, if your current tool incurs payment-gateway commissions on maintenance collections, those recurring costs can often exceed the platform fee over a year, especially for larger societies with high monthly collection volumes. FLATBRIZ offers zero gateway commission on UPI collections, which can lead to significant savings.\n\nTo make this comparison meaningful, could you share your approximate monthly collection amount? This way, we can calculate the potential savings together.	7	{objection:pricing}	f	2026-09-15 05:21:35.683
a01d927d-4361-4412-9cc2-98084146b24b	committee_member	How does the per-flat Dr/Cr ledger work?	The per-flat Dr/Cr ledger in FLATBRIZ allows each flat to maintain its own detailed record of debit (Dr) and credit (Cr) entries. For example, when a maintenance bill is raised, it posts as a debit, while any payments received are recorded as credits. This ledger not only shows the running balance after each entry but also provides transparency, as both the resident and the building admin can view the same information. This eliminates the confusion of a separate "black box" spreadsheet and ensures everyone has access to a full audit trail of financial transactions. Would you like to know more about how this feature can streamline your administrative tasks?	2	{}	f	2026-09-15 05:21:46.687
