230c2ced-24fe-4f92-9103-d135da08cb55	committee_member	Hello	Here's what's most relevant on "Talking to Committee Members":\n\nCommittee members (often treasurers or secretaries) want to know the tool will make their specific\njob easier and won't create more admin work than it saves. Emphasize automatic bill generation,\nthe corpus fund tracking, and the audit trail on the ledger — these directly reduce the manual\nspreadsheet work a treasurer currently does every month, and give them something concrete and\ncredible to present at the AGM.	2	{}	f	2026-09-17 10:51:31.434
e2549002-f5f2-4e1e-8d0b-da3a49338d19	committee_member	How does FLATBRIZ handle maintenance bill payments and gateway fees?	FLATBRIZ handles maintenance bill payments through a UPI-first collection system, which charges zero payment gateway commission. This means that all the money collected stays with the society, avoiding the significant fees that other platforms may impose on each transaction. Additionally, payments are posted directly to the flat's ledger with the UPI transaction reference, eliminating the lag often associated with gateway-routed collections. This streamlined process enhances both financial transparency and administrative control.\n\nHow does your current payment system handle these aspects?	7	{objection:payment_gateway_lag}	f	2026-09-17 10:57:35.922
