tency all the way to the expiration date.\n\nPotency increases with the amount of probiotics consumed. The higher the number,the higher the potency. Potency is measured in CFUs (Colony Forming Units), or live active cultures. People looking for mild daily support should start with a lower number. People with digestive concerns should consider a higher number.\n\nThis combination is one of the most advanced digestive health products available. It supplies a premium blend of digestive enzymes, fiber and acidophilus to form a more complete digestive formula.\n\n## Herbs & Natural Remedies\n\nWhole herbs are usually dried, chopped or ground into powder, and may be processed with water or alcohol for encapsulation. Standardized herbal extracts are made by dissolving herbs in a solvent like water, alcohol or liquid carbon dioxide, resulting in a chemical extract. The goal of standardization is to provide uniformity of a specific constituent that may be biologically active.\n\nIt is an enteric coated to prevent garlic odor. Contains 1100 mg of whole herb which supports cardiovascular health.\n\nGingko can be enjoyed many ways. Ginkgo biloba extract is collected from the dried green leaves of the plant and is available as liquid extracts, capsules, and tablets form. Look for an extract that contains flavonoids and terpenoids on the label, or contains the standardized leaf extract sometimes referred to as GBE (ginkgo biloba extract).\n\nIt was observed that ginkgo can increase blood flow to the eye and improves visual damage in some glaucoma patients. Many herbal remedies given to Glaucoma patients seem to have Ginkgo Biloba in them.\n\nEach serving contains 1000 mg of Cranberry Juice Concentrate. Rich in antioxidants and phytochemicals for healthy immune system, provide dietary support for a healthy urinary tract and reducing risk of cardiovascular disease. A great alternative to high sugar cranberry juice with an easy-to- swallow capsule.\n\n- Korean Ginseng: Modern scientific research and studies suggest that consistent consumption of Korean Ginseng will boost immunity, metabolism, regulates energy levels, improves skin, improves blood circulation and has relaxing effect.\n\n- American Ginseng: American ginseng, has been enjoyed by Native Americans for centuries as a way to support energy, fertility, and digestion. Potent chemicals deep within the root of the plant are responsible for its therapeutic benefits. Polysaccharide glycans and ginsenosides are the most important. They’re two special nutrients that kick starts the energy boost for which ginseng is best known.\n\n- Siberian Ginseng: Siberian ginseng consists of a group of glycosides known as eleutherosides, and known as an adaptogen, which help the body adjust to stressful circumstances, ranging from extreme heat or cold to infections or trauma. In women it supports healthy menstruation, uterine tone and Offering a fertility boost to men.\n\n- Brazilian Ginseng: Used for the treatment of chronic fatigue syndrome, menopausal symptoms, ulcers, anxiety, menstrual problems, impotence, immune support and also as an aphrodisiac.\n\n- Indian Ginseng: Indian ginseng, commonly known as Ashwagandha, is one of the most important herbs in oriental Indian medicine.\n\nThose who use ginseng swear by its effects. Some conditions that ginseng has been used to treat are: Alzheimer's disease, chronic fatigue syndrome, the common cold, diabetes, infertility in males, stress, the flu, fibromyalgia, infection, and atherosclerosis. Bodybuilders and athletes have found ginseng to be a very valuable supplement for a number of reasons. First, ginseng helps the body adapt to higher levels of stress. Next, ginseng has the ability to increase endurance and help recovery rates. Finally, ginseng is a remedy for fatigue and nervous breakdown.	2026-09-23 08:21:50.742	\N	2026-09-23 08:21:50.742	FAQ
