4a299e48-feeb-497e-8171-b6c7ccdecf42	fec71814-41de-4ec3-aab6-9910a3b2e0ca	Find Answers to Frequently Asked Questions | GNC India	## Protein & Fitness\n\nThe average person's body is approximately 18% protein .It forms parts of skin, tendons, muscles, cell membranes, organs and bones. And is involved in creating chemical messengers which provide fuel for growth and serve as a catalyst for maintaining muscle while losing or maintaining weight. Also influence mood and a sense of well-being.\n\nProtein supplements are designed to help meet protein needs if they aren't being met through diet alone .May be more cost effective than getting protein through quality whole-foods alone .In many cases, lower in calories, cholesterol, fat and/or carbohydrates than food sources, particularly non-lean meats. Convenient, and available in many forms such as powders, bars, snacks and ready-to- drink liquids .Offered in a variety of forms, each useful for different goals and at different times in the day.\n\n- Whey is a Fast-absorbing protein. Great for growth and muscle recovery, especially when used with 30-60 minutes after a workout.Source: Cheese\n\n- Casein is a Slow-absorbing protein. Provides a steady release of amino acids over longer periods of time such as while sleeping. Source: Cow's Milk\n\n- Plant Based consists of variety of protein sources, including: rice, hemp, soy and pea. Generally lactose free and often free of other components some find undesirable.Source: Varies\n\n- Egg protein is absorbed at a rate between whey and casein. It is Lactose-free and highly bio-available.Source: Egg Whites\n\nWeight Gainers are products intended for consumption in order to increase the rate of weight gain. Carbohydrates are in a greater amount. Used by people who are facing some difficulty gaining weight in spite of frequent food intake, used for refueling the body's carbohydrate storage for better performance. Mass gainers are more focused on building up the muscle mass. Carbohydrates are in a lesser amount (protein-rich), used by people who want to add lean muscle mass.\n\nGNC offers a few protein product lines to provide a solution for many health/wellness & fitness goals. Let's take a look at our various GNC brand protein product lines, below. Beyond Raw®, GNC Pro Performance® AMP, GNC Pro Performance®, GNC Total Lean™ and GNC Total Lean™ Advanced.\n\nGNC's most advanced protein, Amplified Wheybolic Extreme 60™, has evolved even further to help meet your specific training goals and develops more strength and power. This product is the only whey protein isolate to combine the whey and leucine clinically shown to fuel increased strength and size with additional ingredients proven to amplify power and anabolism. This formula features a protein blend that has been validated in clinical studies to give a 30% increase in strength, increased muscle size and a 100% improvement in exercise efficiency. Using MicroSorb™ Amino Technology, the amino acids added to this formula are pulverized, or "micronized," from large molecules into smaller particles to facilitate faster absorption. AMPed up the protein with a Power Complex featuring an mTOR-stimulating BCAA blend for protein synthesis and added creatine to increase anabolic muscle growth, making this product a combination of 7 products in 1.\n\nGNC is a leader in sports nutrition. As the industry leader in health and wellness supplements, we are passionate about offering our customers the most cutting-edge protein formulas. GNC has superior Protein formulas. Products contain the full amount of Protein stated on the label and is 100% real Protein. GNC proudly stands behind the quality, potency and taste of protein supplements.\n\nGlutamine plays key roles in protein metabolism, cell volumizing , and anti-catabolism. Glutamine's anti- catabolism ability prevents the breakdown of your muscles. This is especially useful for people 'cutting down'. Especially during summer when you're trying to get rid of some body fat without losing any muscle. Glutamine is needed throughout your body for optimal performance. Your small intestines requires the most Glutamine in your body, and your immune system also needs Glutamine because Glutamine levels deplete during workouts, bodybuilders are more susceptible to illnesses - this is why L- Glutamine supplementation is so important, not necessarily to gain more muscle, but for the 'maintenance' effects of L-Glutamine.\n\nYes, Creatine is a natural amino acid present in the body of humans and animals. The human body has 100-115 grams of creatine in the form of creatine phosphate. No negative side effects have been noted in the research with the recommended levels of supplementation.\n\nNo. Creatine draws water from the body to do its work. There is a difference between cell volumization and water retention. Cell volumization leads to more water inside the cells, making the muscle bigger and firmer. Water retention, the process that makes the muscles look smooth, happens outside the muscle cells.\n\n## Vitamins & Minerals\n\nSupplements as generally understood include vitamins, minerals, fibre, fatty acids, or amino acids, among other substances. Nutrition supplements intended to provide nutrients that may otherwise not be consumed in sufficient quantities. Nutrition supplements are a not a substitute to your food but a nutritional plus.\n\nMultivitamins are one of the four foundations of good health; they are combinations of key vitamins, minerals, antioxidants and essential nutrients.\n\nOur wholesome formulas provide powerful greens and absolutely no artificial flavours or sweeteners. These can help customers fill nutritional gaps and achieve a higher level of wellness, energy and fitness. These robust potency formulas are non-GMO, gluten free, vegetarian, soy and dairy free.\n\nRDAs are recommended daily intakes of a nutrient for healthy people. They tell you how much of that nutrient you should get on average each day. RDAs are developed by the Food and Nutrition Board at the Institute of Medicine of the National Academies. They vary by age, gender and whether a woman is pregnant or breastfeeding; so there are many different RDAs for each nutrient. DVs were developed by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to help consumers determine the level of various nutrients in a serving of a product or food in relation to their approximate requirement for it. The label actually provides the %DV so that consumers can see how much (what percentage) a serving of the product contributes to reaching the DV.\n\nThere are a lot of options to choose from when selecting which multivitamin is right for an individual. Consider lifestyle, stage of life, gender, dietary choices and health concerns. Another popular consideration is a multivitamin that releases nutrients all at once or gradually over an extended period of time. Many people consider the source of some of the vitamins in the formulation, or the type.\n\n## Fish Oils & Omegas\n\nFish oil is an oil derived from tissues of fish. Fish oil earned its reputation as a nutritional powerhouse from two fatty acids found within it, EPA and DHA. These heavy hitters are also known as Omega-3s. They're necessary for healthy infants, children and adults.\n\nGNC Fish Oils are sourced from wild, deep-ocean fish. They are ultra-purified and clinical grade, with no prescription required.\n\nEPA, DHA and ALA are all types of omega-3s. EPA and DHA are compounds found in Fish Oil that are very beneficial to the body. It helps support heart health, as well as promotes the health of the brain, joints, eyes and skin.\n\nGNC fish oil is free of mercury, lead, heavy metals & PCB's. We only use high-quality ingredients and raw materials which are rigorously tested before being used. Each product goes through 150+ GNC quality checks including raw materials, purity, and potency and expiration date.\n\nIt is specially coated to help reduce "fishy burps"-guaranteed; not just flavoring to cover it.\n\n## Weight Management\n\nTotal Lean™ is GNC's comprehensive weight management line. Supports healthy body composition and supports healthy weight management .It helps in maintaining muscle mass while losing fat.\n\nTotal Lean™ Advanced is a next level body-toning system designed to tighten and tone, improve fitness and stimulate metabolism and energy for an active lifestyle. GNC Total Lean™ Advanced supports healthy metabolism for lean muscle. Goes beyond weight loss and management. It is consumed by those who want to lose fat & tone up.\n\nGNC Total Lean™ Advanced Lean Shake Burn is a delicious protein with a clinically studied blend shown to burn 3X more calories and supercharge your metabolism for fast, energizing results!*^ This advanced formula features 30 grams of ultra-pure whey protein isolate for lean muscle performance and recovery. With just 11 grams of total carbohydrates per serving, Lean Shake™ Burn is also suitable for low carb diets. Scientifically formulated to deliver an invigorating rush of energy, stimulate your mind and body to jumpstart your day and fuel fat-burning workout.\n\nCaffeine is a bitter and white crystalline compound belonging to a family of chemical compounds called xanthines.Caffeine and its related compounds act as central nervous system and heart muscle stimulants. Caffeine has thermo genic properties and can help support improve physical endurance activity and performance. Caffeine also helps support mental alertness. Caffeine can help in the performance of cognitive tasks and reaction time.\n\nAs a meal replacement mix one serving with 8-10 fl. oz. of cold water. Mix well. Drink two shakes daily while following a healthy reduced calorie meal and exercise program to achieve the best results.\n\nGNC Total Lean™ Lean Shake™ 25 offers a well-balanced blend of high quality protein, fiber, vitamins, minerals, and fat. This great tasting combination makes a healthy addition to you dietary regimen. With 2